    "final_answer": "An engineer may not directly claim that an NMR log measures movable water in the untouched zone after invasion. [KB1] [KB2]\nThe limitation is that NMR logs can be affected by factors such as light-hydrocarbon effects, heavy oil, and calibration errors, which may distort the interpretation of movable water. [KB1]\nComplementary logs such as density, neutron, or acoustic logs can help distinguish between movable and bound fluids in the reservoir. [KB2] [KB3]",
